CORRECTION to this commit message.

Two backticked words were written inside a double-quoted shell string, so the shell ran
them as command substitution before git ever saw them. The paragraph beginning "Two
failures the page caught" should read:

  BarChart keys its categories off `name` and defaults there, not off `date`, so a
  date-only row collapsed every bar onto one empty category and React saw duplicate keys.

The message as committed reads "off  and defaults there, not off Mon Jul 27 23:51:07 EDT
2026" — the empty gap was `name` and the timestamp was `date`.
